Patch 12: expose and loosen the CCSO early-termination tolerance.

Standalone; touches only av2/encoder/pickccso.c.

The 101-feature study measured early_terminate_ccso_search_by_cost as both the
largest single time consumer in the encoder and one of its most efficient
features:

    +31.07% time saving, +0.36% BD-rate, ratio 86.3, against a Speed-2 bar of 30

A ratio of 86 against a bar of 30 is nearly three times the headroom the
feature is required to have, and unclaimed headroom is unclaimed speedup. The
study asked of every feature "does removing it hurt?" but never "could it be
pushed further?" -- so a feature sitting far inside the safe region looks like a
success and is left alone.

That second question has already paid once on this branch. Transform-partition
stationarity pruning was passing at ratio 23.6 when its threshold was loosened;
speedup went from +2.60% to +4.01% and the ratio IMPROVED to 26.7, because the
original setting had been chosen conservatively rather than measured. CCSO is a
much larger target than that one: at roughly a third of encode time, a
proportionally similar gain is worth several percent of total runtime instead of
one.

The mechanism is a single hard-coded scalar in the search loop:

    if (early_terminate_ccso_search && final_filtered_cost != UINT64_MAX &&
        1.001 * final_filtered_cost > last_best_cost)
      goto exit_loops;

1.001 is a 0.1% tolerance, which is close to no tolerance at all: the search
continues unless the current configuration is essentially tied with the best so
far. This patch names it CCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE and sets it to 1.01, a 1%
tolerance.

What this is: one step along a curve, not a tuned value. The ratio must decay as
the tolerance loosens -- the stationarity margin decayed sharply at its third
step, from 26.7 to 14.7 -- and finding where it crosses the bar is exactly what
a sweep is for. Because the constant is now a build-time define, sweeping needs
no patch edits:

    -DCCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE=1.005     halfway
    -DCCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE=1.02      more aggressive
    -DCCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE=1.001     exactly today's shipping behaviour

Suggested arms: 1.005 and 1.01 together bracket the near region cheaply. Run at
Speed 2, where the feature is enabled and where its measurement came from.

Expected direction: more speedup, more BD-rate. Whether the ratio stays above 30
is the whole question. The 1.001 fallback means a failed arm costs a rebuild
rather than a lost patch.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/pickccso.c b/av2/encoder/pickccso.c
index a589842..70508f4 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/pickccso.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/pickccso.c
@@ -25,6 +25,40 @@
 #include "av2/encoder/encoder.h"
 #include "av2/encoder/pickccso.h"
 
+// How much worse than the running best a filtered cost may be before the CCSO
+// search abandons the remaining configurations.
+//
+// This is the single scalar controlling how aggressively CCSO search
+// terminates, and it was hard-coded at 1.001 -- a 0.1% tolerance, which is
+// close to no tolerance at all. The 101-feature study measured the feature it
+// governs as both the largest single time consumer in the encoder and one of
+// the most efficient:
+//
+//     early_terminate_ccso_search_by_cost   +31.07% time   +0.36% BD-rate
+//                                           ratio 86.3 vs a Speed-2 bar of 30
+//
+// A ratio of 86 against a bar of 30 is nearly three times the headroom the
+// feature is required to have, and that headroom is unclaimed speedup. The
+// study asked of every feature "does removing it hurt?" and never asked "could
+// it be pushed further?". Asking the second question of transform-partition
+// stationarity pruning took it from +2.60% to +4.01% speedup while its ratio
+// IMPROVED, 23.6 to 26.7, because its threshold had also been set well inside
+// the safe region.
+//
+// CCSO is a much larger target: it accounts for roughly a third of encode time,
+// so a proportionally similar gain is worth several percent of total runtime
+// rather than one.
+//
+// 1.01 is one step along that curve, not a tuned value -- a 1% tolerance
+// instead of 0.1%. The ratio will decay as this loosens, exactly as the
+// stationarity margin did at its third step, and finding where it crosses the
+// bar is what a sweep is for. Sweep without editing this patch:
+// -DCCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE=1.005 and so on; 1.001 restores current
+// shipping behaviour exactly.
+#ifndef CCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE
+#define CCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE 1.01
+#endif
+
 typedef struct {
   uint8_t final_band_log2;
   int8_t best_filter_offset[CCSO_NUM_COMPONENTS][CCSO_BAND_NUM * 16];
@@ -1609,7 +1643,8 @@ static void derive_ccso_filter(CcsoCtx *ctx, AV2_COMMON *cm, const int plane,
               }
               if (early_terminate_ccso_search &&
                   final_filtered_cost != UINT64_MAX &&
-                  1.001 * final_filtered_cost > last_best_cost)
+                  CCSO_EARLY_TERM_TOLERANCE * final_filtered_cost >
+                      last_best_cost)
                 goto exit_loops;
             }
           }
